    "chunk_size_bytes": 1511,
    "chunk_text": "New Ambassador Saman Chandrasiri presents credentials to Israeli President\n\nNewly appointed Ambassador of Sri Lanka to the State of Israel Saman Chandrasiri presented his Letter of Credence to Israel President Isaac Herzog on 3 August 2026 at Beit HaNassi, the President\u2019s Residence in Jerusalem.\n\nPresident Herzog warmly welcomed Ambassador Chandrasiri and wished him success in his assignment in Israel. During the discussion, the President recalled with warmth the visit undertaken to Sri Lanka by his late father, former President Chaim Herzog, and noted the longstanding friendship between the two countries.\n\nPresident Herzog recognized the positive contribution made by Sri Lankan workers to the Israeli economy and observed that labour relations between Sri Lanka and Israel constitute a mutually beneficial partnership. He also noted that Sri Lanka holds a special place in the hearts of Israeli travellers, who greatly appreciate the country\u2019s natural beauty, hospitality and the memorable experiences offered by Sri Lanka.\n\nAmbassador Chandrasiri conveyed the warm greetings and best wishes of H.E. Anura Kumara Dissanayake, President of Sri Lanka, and the people of Sri Lanka. He expressed Sri Lanka\u2019s interest in further expanding bilateral cooperation, particularly in the fields of agricultural technology, defence and trade. He emphasized that the strong people-to-people relations between the two countries provide a firm foundation for broadening cooperation in areas of mutual interest."
  },
